592
00:23:33,279 --> 00:23:36,749
AND I FELT LIKE MAYBE MODELING
WOULD BE A GOOD STEP INTO IT.

593
00:23:36,749 --> 00:23:39,151
BUT I'M VERY
INTERESTED IN COMEDY.

594
00:23:39,151 --> 00:23:40,753
"SATURDAY NIGHT LIVE,"
CALL ME.

595
00:23:40,753 --> 00:23:41,720
UM... (laughing)

596
00:23:44,423 --> 00:23:45,591
I'M BACK IN THE REAL WORLD,

597
00:23:45,591 --> 00:23:47,259
WHERE I'M TALLER
THAN MOST WOMEN,

598
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:50,129
AND I CAN STILL
DATE ANY GUY I WANT

599
00:23:50,129 --> 00:23:52,364
BECAUSE I'M SHORTER
THAN MOST OF THEM,

600
00:23:52,364 --> 00:23:54,700
AND THAT... IS A GIFT.

601
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:57,469
Men: HEY,
JENASCIA SHOULDA WON!

602
00:23:57,469 --> 00:23:58,604
Man: YOU'RE NOT TOO SHORT.

603
00:23:58,604 --> 00:24:00,306
Jenascia:
THANKS, GUYS.

604
00:24:00,306 --> 00:24:01,540
THANKS.

605
00:24:03,575 --> 00:24:06,679
♪♪♪

606
00:24:06,679 --> 00:24:09,682
April: BEFORE THE SHOW,
I WAS WORKING IN MIAMI BEACH

607
00:24:09,682 --> 00:24:12,017
AS AN ACCOUNT EXECUTIVE
FOR AIRBORNE EXPRESS.

608
00:24:12,017 --> 00:24:14,687
WE BOTH MOVED DOWN TO MIAMI,
PATRICK AND I,

609
00:24:14,687 --> 00:24:17,323
AFTER WE GRADUATED
N.Y.U. TOGETHER.

610
00:24:17,323 --> 00:24:18,991
HE'S THE FIRST LOVE
OF MY LIFE.

611
00:24:18,991 --> 00:24:20,592
I WOULDN'T HAVE THE COURAGE
TO DO WHAT I'M DOING RIGHT NOW

612
00:24:20,592 --> 00:24:22,328
IF IT WASN'T FOR HIM.

613
00:24:22,328 --> 00:24:24,330
HE'S REALLY THE ONE
THAT PUSHED ME

614
00:24:24,330 --> 00:24:27,166
TO PURSUE MY DREAM CAREER.

615
00:24:27,166 --> 00:24:29,201
Patrick: ACTUALLY, WE WERE
WATCHING TELEVISION ONE DAY,

616
00:24:29,201 --> 00:24:30,970
FLIPPED THROUGH THE CHANNELS,
SAW THE SHOW.

617
00:24:30,970 --> 00:24:32,504
WE GOT ONLINE,
FOUND THE APPLICATION,

618
00:24:32,504 --> 00:24:34,139
ENCOURAGED HER TO GO AHEAD
AND DO IT.

619
00:24:34,139 --> 00:24:36,308
April: FOR
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

620
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:37,977
Patrick: I WASN'T SHOCKED
WHEN SHE WAS CHOSEN,

621
00:24:37,977 --> 00:24:41,480
BECAUSE MOST OF THE THINGS
THAT SHE WANTS TO DO IN LIFE

622
00:24:41,480 --> 00:24:43,215
END UP HAPPENING FOR HER.

623
00:24:43,215 --> 00:24:46,385
Martin:
THE WINNER--APRIL!

624
00:24:46,385 --> 00:24:48,654
April: I DON'T THINK I REALLY
KNEW HOW COMPETITIVE I WAS.

625
00:24:48,654 --> 00:24:52,024
Tony: APRIL EXECUTED
THE ROUTINE AMAZINGLY.

626
00:24:52,024 --> 00:24:53,492
Mercedes:
SURPRISE, SURPRISE.

627
00:24:53,492 --> 00:24:54,660
APRIL WON THE CHALLENGE.

628
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:56,729
SHE'S MOST DEFINITELY
A THREAT.

629
00:24:56,729 --> 00:24:59,131
WHEN SHE SEES SOMETHING,
SHE DOES IT PERFECTLY.

630
00:24:59,131 --> 00:25:01,033
SHE'S LIKE A MACHINE.

631
00:25:01,033 --> 00:25:02,735
Yoanna: MY IMPRESSION
OF APRIL IS THIS.

632
00:25:06,372 --> 00:25:08,307
- Mercedes: (suppresses laugh)
- Yoanna: IT'S THE TRUTH.

633
00:25:08,307 --> 00:25:10,142
April: IT WAS VERY HURTFUL
